From 40f5d09e728a18de4ef625b7b38c0d633a5c7b87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:54:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] tp: fix rank0 LoadReady one-shot + load-before-ready
 sequencing

CoordinatorTransport::bootstrap previously re-injected rank0 LoadReady on
every WaitingLoadReady poll iteration. With multi-minute GB10 loads that
produced duplicate LoadReady and aborted the cluster.

Also kimi_k3_dist_generate called do_load() only AFTER bootstrap returned,
so the synthetic rank0 LoadReady could be accepted before weights existed.

Fix:
- bootstrap(on_load) runs rank0 load once after BeginLoad/WaitingLoadReady
- inject rank0 LoadReady exactly once, then poll workers only
- generate passes do_load into bootstrap; 90m phase timeout for GB10 loads
- CPU regression: duplicate LoadReady rejected
---
